Pakistani singers Hamza Malik and Zain Zohaib&rsquo;s collaboration Alfaaz has crossed 50 million streams on Spotify, while its reported chart performance in India and recognition on Genius have added to the song&rsquo;s growing success.
The milestone was highlighted by Malik on his Instagram story, which showed 50,240,450 all-time Spotify streams alongside a celebratory message. The figure reflected the total displayed when the story was posted.
Screengrab: lifewithumzamalik/Instagram
Released in July, Alfaaz brought Malik and Zohaib together on a romantic track whose emotive sound has resonated with listeners. Its continued streaming growth has helped the collaboration reach audiences beyond Pakistan.
The song&rsquo;s reported chart performance has further fuelled its momentum. An Instagram story shared by Zohaib&rsquo;s official music account reported that Alfaaz had reached No&nbsp;1 on Spotify&rsquo;s charts in both India and Pakistan, as well as No&nbsp;39 on Spotify&rsquo;s global chart.
&nbsp;
