Brazil&#8217;s defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted Wednesday he is his country&#8217;s rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile.
Bolsonaro&#8217;s defiance on fleeing to Florida signaled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic runoff election Sunday.
&#8220;I am the elected president, and the criminals who stole Brazil&#8217;s election are part of a criminal organization that has established a tyranny,&#8221; Bolsonaro said in the statement published on his X account, slamming &#8220;electoral fraud.&#8221;
&#8220;I will lead the opposition from here,&#8221; he said. In a subsequent statement, he revised his claim, saying he is the &#8220;leader,&#8221; rather than &#8220;president.&#8221;
Bolsonaro, 45, touched down earlier Wednesday in a private jet at Opa-Locka Executive Airport near Miami.
